- **it_hod → cs_hod/cs_lab1/cs_lab2/cs_lab3/cs_lab4**: All five CS machines respond with 0% packet loss (TTL=63, one router hop via router0). ✅
- **Reverse path cs_hod → it_hod**: Works, 0% packet loss. ✅
- **Router0 interfaces**: eth0 (192.168.1.1/24, IT) and eth1 (192.168.2.1/24, CS) both UP, no errors, forwarding traffic. ✅
- **Router0 routing table**: 192.168.1.0/24 and 192.168.2.0/24 both directly connected, RIP routes to all other subnets intact. ✅
- **IP forwarding on router0**: Enabled (`ip_forward=1`). ✅
- **iptables on router0 and CS hosts**: All chains at ACCEPT policy, no rules. ✅
- **FRR daemons on all three routers**: watchfrr, zebra, ripd, mgmtd, staticd all running normally. ✅
- **switch0 / switch1**: Both bridges in forwarding state on all ports. ✅
- **End-host gateways**: it_hod uses 192.168.1.1, all CS machines use 192.168.2.1 — both correct. ✅
- **RIP tables on router1 and router2**: Complete routes to all subnets including 192.168.1.0/24 and 192.168.2.0/24 present and correct. ✅

